{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 108, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 3 removed, edge 5 is a major remaining path into the output node, so deleting it cripples the cell (experiments 70 and 72 show drops of 6 to 75 points)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is already absent, edge 3 carries much more of the signal into node 3, so removing it hurts far more (experiments 82 and 84)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is missing, edge 4 is one of only two inputs to the output node, so removing it is much more damaging (experiment 42: -5.5/-11.8/-15.3)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 5, node 1 feeds the output only through edge 4, and removing edge 0 cuts off that conv path (experiment 94: drops of 5.5 to 15 points)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op on the first edge with a 3x3 conv adds learnable capacity where it was missing (experiments 18 and 24 are large gains)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping pooling for a conv on the direct input-to-output edge gains much more than swapping in a conv for a 1x1 conv or for a cell that already has convs (experiments 2 vs 3, 7)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "When the cell already has a 3x3 conv on edge 0, an extra conv on edge 5 adds little or hurts (experiments 12 and 13 are negative, versus gains elsewhere)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning an absent edge into a conv adds both a new path and learnable capacity, which beats replacing an existing conv (experiment 61 gains 5 to 15 points)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a parameter-free skip costs much less than removing a conv on edge 0, and can even help skip-heavy cells (experiments 87, 95 vs 86, 92)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pooling on edge 4 contributes little useful signal, so removing it is roughly neutral or positive, unlike removing a conv on edge 4 (experiments 36, 38, 41 vs 42, 43)."}], "tok": 30921, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_co